 parent chain, which the setup's single commit does not hold; the cited test
 builds one by committing three times onto one branch, each commit taking the
 tip the one before it left (Phase 17b1 of `../port-plan.md`). The cited
 test also covers `-S` reporting more than one commit, and the `~N` and `^N`
 non-syntaxes, where the tool reports `error: Invalid refspec <rev>` and the
 port reports `error: Refspec '<rev>' not found` (`cli-surface.md`, "P1"); the
 same repository serves all three.

