expect-stderr: contains "error: Rev name 'bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb' looks like a checksum"
ref-expect-exit: 1
ref-expect-stdout: empty
ref-expect-stderr: contains "error: Rev name 'bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb' looks like a checksum"
oracle: exit-status stdout-text stderr-text refs-bytes
outcome: refused-both
severity: interop
spec: format-reference.md#object-store-layout
note: a branch name of 64 lowercase hex characters is the shape resolution reads
 as a checksum, so a ref carrying it is reachable by no revision. Both refuse it
 in the same words at the same step, and `refs-bytes` states that neither wrote
 the ref. `inventory` is no oracle here: the tool writes the tree and the commit
 object before it reads the branch name, so the refusal leaves them in
 `objects/`, where the port publishes a transaction's objects at commit and
 publishes none (`cli-surface.md`, "P2").

