run: commit --repo=$REPO -b conformance -s x --timestamp=1234567890 $TREE
expect-exit: 1
expect-stdout: empty
expect-stderr: equals "error: Could not parse '1234567890'"
ref-expect-exit: 1
ref-expect-stdout: empty
ref-expect-stderr: equals "error: Could not parse '1234567890'"
oracle: exit-status stdout-text stderr-text refs-bytes inventory
outcome: refused-both
severity: interop
spec: format-reference.md#commit
note: a bare count of seconds is not a timestamp to either reader; the `@` form
 is what states one. Both refuse it in the same words and neither writes a ref or
 publishes an object.

