family: M10
subcommand: commit
cell: commit/metadata-forms
setup: repo tree
outcome: full
severity: interop
identity: full
evidence: ostrya_cli::cli::commit_metadata_matches_the_tool
spec: format-reference.md#commit
note: the 236 accepted GVariant value forms and the 170 refused ones, each its
 own invocation, each held to the tool by commit checksum or by the refusal
 text, and each held to its own side of the reader by an absolute exit status. The set covers the reader's edges: a bytestring ending at its first NUL,
 the one-member tuple's comma, the lower-case exponent marker, the decimal
 subnormal refusal, the hexadecimal subnormal a body states exactly, a
 hexadecimal mantissa past 32 digits, the object-path and signature checks,
 `nan` and the infinities, the binary literal, the reader the target type picks,
 and the nesting cap at the level past the one both readers take. It covers the
 escape tables as well: every short escape a string and a bytestring take, the
 line continuation a backslash before a line feed makes, a unicode escape that
 names a character, a character written through as itself, each radix prefix in
 either case, a digit outside the radix, the range edge of each narrow integer
 type, each remaining type keyword, the signature bodies the type scanner takes
 and refuses, the characters a declaration ends at, an array whose element type
 comes from a later element, and the character class an object-path element
 takes. Several hold a single quote, which a `run:` line consumes, so the set
 stands in the cited test.

