family: M10
subcommand: commit
cell: commit/statoverride-mode-reader
setup: repo tree
outcome: lossy
severity: interop
identity: not-required
loss: the value dialect. The tool reads the field through a C `double`, so it
 takes a hexadecimal literal, a decimal point, and an exponent as well, and
 converts a value past the 32-bit range to `0x80000000`; the port reads the
 documented format alone. The first cited test states ten such fields, each
 landing on a different commit in the two implementations at exit 0 in both,
 and holds the tool's `4294967296`, `1e100`, `inf`, `nan`, and `4294967295`
 against the commit the literal `2147483648` gives, which is the value both
 implementations read for `0x80000000`. `4294967295` and `-1` are the two
 spellings of `0xFFFFFFFF`, so each renames the type and draws the refusal the
 cell above states, where the tool commits at exit 0. The forms sit outside the
 documented format and the out-of-range conversion is platform-defined, so the
 port does not reproduce them (`cli-surface.md`, "Scope of CLI compatibility").
evidence: ostrya_cli::cli::commit_statoverride_divergences_stand_as_recorded,
 ostrya_cli::cli::commit_statoverride_matches_the_tool
