note: two forced faults state the order. A key that cannot sign leaves the ref
 at the checksum it held, with no commit object published and no `.commitmeta`;
 a `refs/heads` that cannot be written leaves the commit object beside its
 `.commitmeta` and writes no ref. The two word the write failure differently, so
 the claim is the state each leaves.

