evidence: ostrya_cli::cli::commit_sign_replace_and_append_match_the_tool
spec: format-reference.md#signing-details
note: six runs onto one orphan checksum. `--add-detached-metadata-string`
 replaces the whole stored dict and a signing option appends to what stands, so
 a signature survives a later signing run and not a later replace, which the
 cited test reads out of the key listing after each run. `--orphan` resolves no
 parent, so `--skip-if-unchanged` beside it compares against nothing and the run
 signs like any other: the stored dict grows by one element.

