evidence: ostrya_cli::cli::commit_gpg_sign_matches_the_tool
spec: format-reference.md#commit
note: a `--gpg-sign` selector under eight bytes draws `error: Unable to lookup
 key ID <KEY-ID>: GPGME: Invalid value` without a key lookup, whatever it would
 have named. The cited test walks the empty selector and five short ones, four
 of which are user-id substrings that a lookup would resolve, so no key is
 picked from a selector the tool refuses. Eight bytes and longer reach the
 lookup: a user-id substring naming the key signs, which the stored
 `ostree.gpgsigs` element states, and one naming nothing draws the "No gpg key
 found" line. Each refusal is held at exit 1, with the line the record quotes
 and with no ref written. A `run:` line cannot state it: the harness has no setup that
 generates a GnuPG home directory.

